OL-NS-04(c), and POL-NS-11 if it cannot be run), and the fee itself does not depend on your presence — POL-NS-01 and POL-NS-06 both operate 'whether or not the rider was present'. A clause therefore resolves the point, so the POL-NS-09(b) trigger is not engaged, and no other POL-NS-09 trigger is present: both counterparty-dispute counters are 0, your no_show_disputes_30d is 1 (the limb reads 3), the anti-farming check is clear, and every artifact carrying a deciding fact is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so limb (e) is not reached. The disputed fee is not held.\n\nTo the driver: POL-NS-07 fixes your payout at 80 percent of the net cancellation fee in force — 0.80 × $4.50 = $3.60, which is also the figure stated on the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-03307). The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 0 against the absolute threshold of 4, so the accompanying rate test cannot bite either.\n\nNo artifact is impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08: the arrival event and the nearest trace fix agree to the second, the trace has no gaps and 100 percent coverage, the chat log holds the 2 messages the trip record records, and the cancellation-fee line reconciles with the figure the resolution rule produces. The only missing artifact, the traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-03307-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), is not relied on for any finding, and the single continuous in-geofence run means no accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) was ever needed. Confidence is 0.90, against a cap of 1.0 set by the weight-1.0 artifacts the finding rests on. The money moved (SGD 3.60) is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold. Ruling: DRIVER_COMPENSATION — the $4.50 charge stands and the platform pays the driver $3.60."
